==============================================================================
(3) k=12 cut(I) failure is OUTSIDE the binding regime
==============================================================================
  E=[0..10,12]: p0=0.645181 > p0(consec_12)=0.624114  BUT cap_12=0.857143
     -> p0(E)=0.6452 < cap_12=0.8571: NO cap violation. And k>=11 closes via THM-535 floor route.

==============================================================================
(4) does p0 depend only on the difference-multiset?
==============================================================================
  k=7: 450 difference-multisets shared by >1 distinct primitive set
     COUNTEREXAMPLE: [(0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 8), (0, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8)] share diffmult but p0 differs: [0.03197278911564626, 0.016666666666666666]
     COUNTEREXAMPLE: [(0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 9), (0, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9)] share diffmult but p0 differs: [0.02857142857142857, 0.032086167800453515]
  => p0 is NOT a function of the difference-multiset  (checked 3 colliding classes)
